      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "'Nos' is the reflexive pronoun for nosotros: 'Nos levantamos a las siete' (We get up at seven)."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Yo me ____ (ducharse) por la mañana.' (I shower in the morning.)",
      "correct": "ducho",
      "explanation": "'Me ducho' — the yo form of ducharse in the present. The reflexive pronoun 'me' goes before the conjugated verb."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Ellos se ____ (acostar) a las once.' (They go to bed at eleven.)",
      "correct": "acuestan",
      "explanation": "'Se acuestan' — they go to bed. Acostarse has a stem change: o→ue in the present (ellos se acuestan)."
    },
    {
      "type": "exercise",
      "question": "Which of these is a reflexive verb for daily routine?",
      "options": [
        "comer",
        "hablar",
        "despertarse",
        "trabajar"
      ],
      "correct": 2,
      "explanation": "'Despertarse' (to wake up) is reflexive — the action reflects back on the subject: yo me despierto."
    },
